Eventually, that was the route I tried to take, rather than
digging down or sideways.  HOWEVER....

Other duties called, so I saved the game just after the
guard asked "Pardon me, but who are you?"  Then when I
came back later and resumed, weird things happened.
The guard started flickering in and out, I turned into
a black square instead of an elf, some of the hallway
squares turned black, and I was trapped in a short,
zigzag hallway, isolated from the rest of the dungeon,
while an invisible guard somewhere crooned "Move along,
now.  Move along, now."  Then a message box popped up
saying "Imaginary hallway error.  Please report this
to the nethack devteam."  Then the program crashed.

On attempting to recover, I got: "Nethack: This
program has performed an illegal memory access and
will be shut down."

On attempting to start a new game, I got "Files
already in progress from previous game; cannot
start new game."

I was eventually able to resume the crashed game,
and quit before the illegal memory access occurred,
thus clearing-out the old, corrupted in-progress
game files so I could start a new game.

So, looks there's a bug in Nethack, such that if
you save immediately after a guard asks "who are
you?", the game may crash on resume.

